#: R/ihcheterogeneity.b.R
msgid ""
"Slope of the difference on the mean of the two measurements (the region and "
"the reference), with heteroscedasticity-robust (HC3) standard errors; p is "
"unadjusted. Measurement error alone tilts a slope on the reference value "
"downwards and a slope on the region value upwards, so a difference is "
"treated as changing with the level only when its slope differs from zero (p "
"below 0.05 divided by the number of comparisons) in the same direction on "
"all three: the reference value, the region value and their mean (Krouwer "
"2008). Such a difference is judged at the 5th and 95th percentiles of the "
"mean, against the margin at the comparison mean taken as fixed; it can stop "
"a difference from being ruled out but never shows it to be material (Bland & "
"Altman 1995, 1999)."
msgstr ""

#: R/ihcheterogeneity.b.R
msgid ""
"Slope of the difference on the mean of the two regions compared, with "
"heteroscedasticity-robust (HC3) standard errors; p is unadjusted. Unequal "
"measurement error between regions can produce a slope, so here a slope can "
"stop a difference from being ruled out but never shows it to be material. "
"When p is below 0.05 divided by the number of comparisons, the difference is "
"also judged at the 5th and 95th percentiles of that level (Bland & Altman "
"1999)."
msgstr ""

